      "message": "The `CommandLineManager` class is an example of the \"Object-Oriented Noun\" anti-pattern. It holds no complex mutating state and is only instantiated once to immediately parse arguments and yield a struct.\n\n**Suggestion:** Drop the class entirely. Convert `ParseCommandLine` into a standalone free function that returns `std::expected\u003cCmdLine, ...\u003e` or `std::optional\u003cCmdLine\u003e`. This removes the class declaration, constructor boilerplate, and the `GetCommandLine()` getter, drastically flattening the `main.cc` logic.",
