      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s a fix generated by Gemini. Double-check that it is correct and compiles and works correctly:\n\n----\n\nBy removing the `CommandLineManager` class, we eliminate unnecessary object-oriented boilerplate for something that is inherently a procedural, one-time operation.\n\nTo do this, we can move the helper functions (`PrintHelp`, `ParseHex`) and the core parsing logic (`ParseCommandLine`) into an anonymous namespace. This makes them internal to `iap_tool.cc` without needing a class scope. `ParseCommandLine` is then updated to directly return an `std::optional\u003cCmdLine\u003e`.\n\nHere is the refactored top half of `iap_tool.cc` incorporating these changes, along with the added scope braces `{}` in the `switch` statement to prevent compiler warnings about variable initialization.\n\n### The Refactored `iap_tool.cc`\n\n```c\n// Copyright 2026 The ChromiumOS Authors\n// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be\n// found in the LICENSE file.\n\n#include \u003cgetopt.h\u003e\n#include \u003cunistd.h\u003e\n\n#include \u003ccharconv\u003e\n#include \u003ccstddef\u003e\n#include \u003ccstdint\u003e\n#include \u003ccstdio\u003e\n#include \u003ccstdlib\u003e\n#include \u003cformat\u003e\n#include \u003ciostream\u003e\n#include \u003coptional\u003e\n#include \u003cstring\u003e\n#include \u003cstring_view\u003e\n#include \u003cvector\u003e\n\n#include \"file_control.h\"\n#include \"iap_control.h\"\n#include \"utility.h\"\n\nstruct CmdLine {\n  uint16_t vid;\n  uint16_t pid;\n  std::string file_path;\n};\n\nvoid SetProgressBar(size_t progress, size_t total_size);\n\nnamespace {\n\nvoid PrintHelp(const char *program_name) {\n  std::print(R\"(Usage: {} [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n  -F, --file \u003cpath\u003e   Path to the firmware binary (Required)\n  -V, --vid \u003chex\u003e     USB Vendor ID (default: 0x04F3)\n  -P, --pid \u003chex\u003e     USB Product ID (default: 0x0910)\n  -h, --help          Show this help message\n)\",\n             program_name);\n}\n\nstd::optional\u003cuint16_t\u003e ParseHex(std::string_view strv) {\n  if (strv.empty()) return std::nullopt;\n\n  // Strip standard hex prefixes\n  if (strv.starts_with(\"0x\") || strv.starts_with(\"0X\")) {\n    strv.remove_prefix(2);\n  }\n\n  uint16_t val;\n  auto [ptr, ec] \u003d\n      std::from_chars(strv.data(), strv.data() + strv.size(), val, 16);\n\n  if (ec \u003d\u003d std::errc() \u0026\u0026 ptr \u003d\u003d strv.data() + strv.size()) {\n    return val;\n  }\n\n  return std::nullopt;\n}\n\nstd::optional\u003cCmdLine\u003e ParseCommandLine(int argc, char *argv[]) {\n  CmdLine cmd{elan::kBootVid, elan::kBootPid, \"\"};\n\n  // Define long options\n  static struct option long_options[] \u003d {\n      {\"file\", required_argument, nullptr, \u0027F\u0027},\n      {\"vid\", required_argument, nullptr, \u0027V\u0027},\n      {\"pid\", required_argument, nullptr, \u0027P\u0027},\n      {\"help\", no_argument, nullptr, \u0027h\u0027},\n      {nullptr, 0, nullptr, 0}};\n\n  int opt;\n  while ((opt \u003d getopt_long(argc, argv, \"hF:V:P:\", long_options, nullptr)) !\u003d -1) {\n    switch (opt) {\n      case \u0027h\u0027:\n        PrintHelp(argv[0]);\n        std::exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n      case \u0027F\u0027:\n        cmd.file_path \u003d optarg;\n        break;\n      case \u0027V\u0027: {\n        if (auto val \u003d ParseHex(optarg)) {\n          cmd.vid \u003d *val;\n        } else {\n          LogErr(\"Invalid VID format: {}\\n\", optarg);\n          return std::nullopt;\n        }\n        break;\n      }\n      case \u0027P\u0027: {\n        if (auto val \u003d ParseHex(optarg)) {\n          cmd.pid \u003d *val;\n        } else {\n          LogErr(\"Invalid PID format: {}\\n\", optarg);\n          return std::nullopt;\n        }\n        break;\n      }\n      default:\n        PrintHelp(argv[0]);\n        return std::nullopt;\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (cmd.file_path.empty()) {\n    LogErr(\"Error: Missing required argument \u0027--file\u0027\\n\");\n    PrintHelp(argv[0]);\n    return std::nullopt;\n  }\n\n  return cmd;\n}\n\n}  // namespace\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]) {\n  elan::IapControl iap_ctrl;\n\n  // 1. Replaced the class instantiation with a direct function call\n  auto cmd_line \u003d ParseCommandLine(argc, argv);\n  if (!cmd_line) {\n    LogErr(\"[IAP] Failed to parse command line\\n\");\n    return EXIT_FAILURE;\n  }\n\n  if (auto res \u003d iap_ctrl.Initialize(cmd_line-\u003evid, cmd_line-\u003epid); !res) {\n    LogErr(\"[IAP] Device initialization failed: {}\\n\",\n           elan::ToString(res.error()));\n    return EXIT_FAILURE;\n  }\n\n  LogInfo(\"[IAP] File Path: {}\\n\", cmd_line-\u003efile_path);\n\n  // ... (The rest of main and SetProgressBar remain unchanged) ...\n\n```\n\n### Why this is better:\n\n* **Reduced Cognitive Load:** A reader opening `main()` immediately sees a function call `ParseCommandLine` instead of a class instantiation and a subsequent getter method.  \n* **No Unnecessary State:** The `CommandLineManager` was holding `cmd_line_` in memory unnecessarily for the lifetime of the object. Now, the parsed struct is built, returned by value, and safely deposited directly into `main()`.  \n* **Cleaner Scope:** Wrapping the helpers in an anonymous namespace ensures they cannot be accidentally linked or called from outside this specific `.cc` file.",
